      <title>Kodiak commercial trawlers pause fishing while Board of Fisheries considers trawl proposals</title>
      <link>https://www.kmxt.org/news/2026-03-18/kodiak-commercial-trawlers-pause-fishing-while-board-of-fisheries-considers-trawl-proposals</link>
      <description>The Kodiak-based trawl fleet is pausing its fishing for pollock in state waters for three days while the Alaska Board of Fisheries weighs in on proposed tighter restrictions for trawl fishermen, including monitoring of seafloor contact in and around state waters.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.kmxt.org/news/2026-03-18/kodiak-commercial-trawlers-pause-fishing-while-board-of-fisheries-considers-trawl-proposals</guid>
